(292,'D4277','PERIODONTIC','free soft tissue graft procedure (including recipient and donor surgical sites) first tooth, implant, or edentulous tooth position in graft','One (1) per tooth per lifetime','Narrative/remarks describing the procedure and tooth numbers are required with the claim. The patient must be age eighteen (18) or older.','Tooth identification'),
(293,'D4278','PERIODONTIC','free soft tissue graft procedure (including recipient and donor surgical sites) each additional contiguous tooth, implant, or edentulous tooth position in same graft site','One (1) per tooth per lifetime','Narrative/remarks describing the procedure and tooth numbers are required with the claim. The patient must be age eighteen (18) or older.','Tooth identification'),
(294,'D4283','PERIODONTIC','autogenous connective tissue graft procedure (including donor and recipient surgical sites) - each additional contiguous tooth, implant, or edentulous tooth position in same graft site','Not a covered benefit','None','None'),
(295,'D4285','PERIODONTIC','non-autogenous connective tissue graft procedure (including recipient surgical site and donor material)- each additional contiguous tooth, implant, or edentulous tooth position in same graft site','Not a covered benefit','None','None'),
(296,'D4286','PERIODONTIC','removal of non-resorbable barrier','Not a covered benefit','None','None'),
(297,'D4322','PERIODONTIC','splint - intra -coronal; natural teeth or prosthetic crowns','Not a covered benefit','None','None'),
(298,'D4323','PERIODONTIC','splint - extra -coronal; natural teeth or prosthetic crowns','Not a covered benefit','None','None'),
(299,'D4341','PERIODONTIC','periodontal scaling and root planing - four (4) or more teeth per quadrant','One (1) per quadrant in a two (2) year period, age eighteen (18) and older.','Periodontal scaling and root planing may be used as a definitive treatment in some stages of periodontal disease and/or as a part of pre-surgical procedures in others. D4341 is a benefit when four (4) or more teeth in a quadrant have periodontal pockets measuring four (4) mm or greater.\r\nD4342 is a benefit when less than four\r\n(4) teeth in a quadrant have periodontal pockets measuring four (4) mm or greater. Once every two (2) years. Patient must be eighteen (18) years and older. Must demonstrate radiographic alveolar bone loss and subgingival calculus to be a benefit.\r\nNote: If member has diabetes, CAD, stroke or is pregnant and is enrolled in Oral Health for Total Health, D4341 or D4342 may be covered once per quadrant every twenty-four (24) months.','Quadrant identification'),
(300,'D4342','PERIODONTIC','periodontal scaling and root planing - one (1) to three (3) teeth per quadrant','One (1) per quadrant in a two (2) year period, age eighteen (18) and older.','Refer to details listed for Code D4342.','Tooth identification'),
(301,'D4346','PERIODONTIC','scaling in presence of generalized moderate or severe gingival inflammation - full mouth, after oral evaluation','Twice (2) per calendar year age 13 and older.','This code will be interchangeable with code D1110. This code will be covered as a preventative service and will share the same frequency limitations, processing guidelines, relationship to other codes, provider/ member liability as code D1110.\r\nNote: If member is enrolled in Oral Health for Total Health, D1110/D1120 or D4346 or D4910 is covered once every three months.','None'),
(302,'D4355','PERIODONTIC','full mouth debridement to enable a comprehensive periodontal evaluation and diagnosis on a subsequent visit','Not a covered benefit.','Note: If member is enrolled in Oral Health for Total Health, D4355 may be covered one (1) every twenty-four (24) months.','None'),
(303,'D4381','PERIODONTIC','localized delivery of antimicrobial agents via a controlled release vehicle into diseased crevicular tissue, per tooth','Benefit for Federal plan only.','One (1) treatment per tooth per twenty- four (24) months. Up to three (3) teeth per quadrant or ten (10) teeth overall with 5-6 mm pocket depths and bleeding on probing with, or subsequent to active and maintained periodontal treatment. This treatment should not be used to treat generalized disease. Not covered for treatment of periodontal abscess or in conjunction with periodontal surgery. If denied for above criteria not being met, it is a member liability. Patient must be eighteen (18) years and older.','Detailed Narrative\r\nTooth/teeth identification(s)'),
(304,'D4910','PERIODONTIC','Periodontal maintenance','Two (2) per calendar year in addition to regular prophy.','Periodontal maintenance includes removal of the bacterial plaque and calculus from supragingival, and subgingival regions, site-specific scaling and root planing where indicated, and polishing the teeth. If new or recurring periodontal disease appears, additional diagnostic and treatment procedures must be considered. Periodontal maintenance is covered two (2) times per calendar year following surgical and definitive non-surgical therapy. The patient must be age eighteen (18) or older.\r\nPeriodontal maintenance should not be performed on same day as periodontal surgery.\r\nNote: If member is enrolled in Oral Health for Overall Health, D1110/D1120 or D4346 or D4910 may\r\nbe covered One (1) every three (3) months.','None'),
(305,'D4920','PERIODONTIC','unscheduled dressing change (by someone other than treating dentist or their staff)','Not a covered benefit.','None','None'),
(306,'D4921','PERIODONTIC','gingival irrigation with a medicinal agent- per quadrant','Not a covered benefit.','None','None'),
(307,'D4999','PERIODONTIC','unspecified periodontal procedure, by report','By report.','Individual Consideration. Detailed narrative required','Detailed narrative'),
